      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A novel and efficient rhodium-catalyzed procedure for the preparation of silyl-substituted indenones has been developed. Using silanes and internal alkynes as the substrates, in the presence of CO, good to excellent yields of the desired indenones were isolated. A wide range of functional groups, encompassing esters, amines, nitriles and halides, is compatible in this system."},
